# Conventions

See [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).

## Plugin

- App id `eduardkolotushin-forecast-app`
- Nested panel id `eduardkolotushin-forecast-panel`
- Nested datasource id `eduardkolotushin-forecast-datasource`
- Backend executable `gpx_forecast` (app process and a copy under `forecast-datasource/`)
- Go 1.26+

## API

- `POST /forecast` returns new points and optional `lower`/`upper`; do not mutate inputs
- `cacheKey` / `needTrain` / `retrain` skip the train query when a snapshot exists
- Panel forecasts each numeric series independently
- Panel `showInterval` gates `level`; training uses a from/to query, not the visible range; forecast uses a from/to window (`ForecastRange`)
- Train rewrite is type-keyed in the overlay frontend (Prom / OpenSearch / Postgres / Druid); `pkg/` has no Prom/OS/PG **datasource** clients (pgx snapshot store is allowed)
- Snapshot DSN: `FORECAST_STORE_*` (Grafana 12.4+ does not forward host env by default), then `GF_PLUGIN_EDUARDKOLOTUSHIN_FORECAST_APP_*` / `GF_PLUGIN_EDUARDKOLOTUSHIN_FORECAST_DATASOURCE_*` / GrafanaCfg, then jsonData; CI merges `conf/forecast.ini.template` (app and datasource plugin sections)
- Datasource `QueryData` Restores by `cacheKey` and emits forecast / lower / upper; miss is an error (overlay trains). Do not query other datasources from `pkg/`
- Overlay Mixed: cacheKey and train use metric targets only; Forecast datasource frames are not fitted or plotted
- Forecast query editor does not auto-fill; Copy source from query A is opt-in for `sourceTargets` only
- Overlay options New alert rule navigates to Grafana `/alerting/new` with live panel queries and dashboard/panel annotations; do not ship rules
- Pre-size Go slices to the request/window length

## Quality

- Table-driven tests next to the resource handler and `QueryData`
- Table-driven frontend tests next to train rewrite, extract, cache fingerprint, mixed frames, forecast-query `cacheKey`, and overlay New alert rule defaults
- No drive-by refactors
- Keep Grafana scaffold files under `.config/` unless a plugin-tools upgrade requires it
